WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.050
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:06.980
<i>Last week on Frankenstein Family...</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.650
<i>Aisuri-neesan never listened to me.</i>

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.990
<i>When I told her to stop going 
out looking like a spider,</i>

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.600
<i>she got all pissy and said "you can 
do all the housework yourself."</i>

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.310
<i>That's no problem! I can do it all by myself.</i>

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:27.330
<i>I'm a genius, after all.</i>

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.510
<i>And when I went shopping, I ran into 
this really nice girl named Sumire-chan!</i>

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.050
<i>But the next thing I knew, I'd gotten lost!</i>

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.900
<i>I may be a genius, but I have 
a lousy sense of direction...</i>

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.270
<i>My siblings came to look for me, 
and eventually they found me.</i>

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.690
<i>It made me feel really grateful to have them.</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:42.450
<b>#3: Reality</b>

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.780
Yes. Yes.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:45.930
I understand.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.130
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:51.750
Goodbye.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.940
I need to go to the mainland 
tomorrow to meet someone I know.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.430
Since when do you know 
anyone on the mainland?

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.430
Who is it?

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.820
Anyone we know?

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.390
I dug through some of my old notes

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.460
and got in touch with my old tutor.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.650
What are you gonna do with
 some old tutor of yours?

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:20.670
What we need right now is an 
adult willing to help us out.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.680
You intend to go by yourself?

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.950
Could become a dog at any time

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.910
Wild and reckless

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.500
Airheaded, prone to spacing out

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.980
You'll fall off a cliff again.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.730
That was an accident!

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.490
Should I go with you?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.450
N-No way!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.130
If you accidentally show your 
tail, we'll get in trouble.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:55.000
And Aisuri-neesan will definitely 
cause trouble, so I can't take her.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.510
Hey!

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:00.180
So I was thinking I'd have 
to take Ashisu-neesan.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:05.740
I thought if I had to, I could use her 
ability to get the teacher to believe me.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.470
It's decided.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.470
I'll go.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.700
Things sure are different in the big city...

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.030
Let's go that way!

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.300
You'll get lost again like that.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.040
But I thought you hated being outside.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.630
Why did you come with me?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.510
I would prefer it if you didn't die.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.760
You're making too much of it.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.430
So, do you know how to get there?

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.710
Don't worry!

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.680
Hey! Excuse me!

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.770
Huh?

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.850
Um...

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.670
Excuse me!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.160
This isn't how I imagined it...

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.930
Hey there, sonny.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.500
Could you hire me a taxi?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.290
I lost all my money...

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.540
Don't.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:20.650
Neesan?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.640
She's a con artist.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.860
I'll show you how to get there.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.780
How do I get to Mt. Hakuun?!

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.800
<i>He just needs to take the subway.</i>

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.530
<i>Did this boy come to the city all alone?</i>

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.330
<i>Where is that?</i>

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.170
<i>It's just one bus away.</i>

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:59.210
<i>The subway station is right there.</i>

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.660
<i>Oh, poor little boy...</i>

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:04.810
So noisy.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.280
Come on.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.200
<i>She really knows how to use her powers...</i>

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.650
<i>Even though she spends 
so much time indoors...</i>

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.250
<i>The train is arriving on 
the second platform.</i>

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.240
<i>Please watch your step.</i>

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.720
Watch your wallet.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.440
'Scuse me!

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:04.200
The city's nothing like I expected.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.340
Tanisu-kun?

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.590
You remember me?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.500
I couldn't believe you contacted me.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.720
Yeah. We're in a little trouble.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.600
What happened?

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.120
Let's talk it out over lunch.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:56.850
Okay.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.840
Here you are.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:16.800
Enjoy!

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:55.610
Delicious!

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.420
And who's this young lady?

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:03.780
This is my big sister, Suishi!

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.520
She's not exactly the expressive type, so...

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.270
Are you here about her?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.780
Ah, no. This is how she always is.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.780
Then...

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.790
<i>How should I explain?</i>

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.400
Put it in your own words.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:22.170
I'm not the friendly type, 
so I'd make her uncomfortable.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.040
Um...

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.760
Our parents were researchers,

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:33.070
and they did experiments on my siblings 
for a program they were running.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:37.010
Then they were taken away 
by the police, and...

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:39.300
Why did you come to me?

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.520
I don't have any adults I can count on.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.520
I see...

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:53.590
Even so, I don't see how I could help you.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.530
You may have forgotten this by now,

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:02.130
but I still remember it clear as day.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.170
I'm so bored!

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.460
It's all too darn easy.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.880
Teach me something I don't already know.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.300
We're done here. You can go home now.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.320
<i>You can't even teach an eight-year-old kid?</i>

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:26.280
<i>You've got that fancy degree,
 but that's all you got?</i>

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.480
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.850
<i>If you can't handle elementary schoolers, 
you can go teach kindergarten!</i>

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:36.360
I... was once considered 
the top of the elite...

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:40.300
And you humiliated me, just like that.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.850
Genius, my ass!

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:43.450
You've been scientifically modified!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.020
No, I'm not!

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.870
Yes, I'm sure of it!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.500
I knew it was strange...

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.210
Don't underestimate humans,

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:01.390
you botched Frankenstein!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.850
I'm... not...

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.830
Let me offer a bit of advice 
to my dear, former pupil.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:11.770
Go to the government.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.560
You'll make a fine guinea pig.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:22.930
Monsters. You're all monsters.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.530
It seems we're finished here.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.150
Let's go, Tanisu.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.130
Serves you right.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:39.170
That's right... you're on 
your third boyfriend.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:45.030
It was that pride of yours that 
made the previous two dump you.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.390
Even so, you have one 
true friend, named Rijen.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:54.770
Her house isn't far from here.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:58.710
Wh-What <i>are</i> you?

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:01.900
There's no need to worry.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.800
As long as you don't do anything to us,

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:09.060
we won't harm you.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:13.670
Thank you for the meal, 
"kindergarten teacher."

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.900
Did you know this would happen?

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.150
She's no different from 
the other city people.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.070
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:56.770
Am I really a genius?

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.840
You are a genius.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.130
You're just still a child.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:27.690
Hey!

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.000
Thanks for before.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.050
Um...

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.450
Sumire!

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.260
Hello, Sumire.

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:45.220
I'm...

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:50.330
<i>Monsters. You're all monsters.</i>

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.180
Kanisu.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.680
My name is Kanisu.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.730
That's a strange name.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.120
Are you foreign?

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.640
Yeah.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.510
I see!

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:11.570
If you need anything, call me, okay?

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:13.380
Here!

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.000
Phone:

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.000
Sumire

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.000
Bye-bye!

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.110
Who was that?

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.910
A new friend!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.330
She was being genuine.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.220
Phone

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.220
Sumire

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:39.230
Yeah.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:22.960
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.540
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.960
<b>Today's theme is...</b>

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.960
<i>Today's theme is...</i>

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.120
Let's bring out the board again!

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:24.830
Let's get going!

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:25.260
Yeah.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:25.580
There!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.090
Dun-dun-dun!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.630
"Who's your favorite character 
in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>?"

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:31.920
Pick your favorite?

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:36.300
<b>Who's your favorite character
in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>?</b>

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:36.300
<b>Aisuri
Mori Nanako</b>

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:36.300
<b>Suishi
Ikuta Yoshiko</b>

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:36.300
<b>Tanisu
Sugiyama Riho</b>

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:32.620
Your favorite!

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.160
I have one.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.390
For me, it's Aisuri-neesan.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.140
Oh, really?

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:42.980
We have no one to rely on. 
We don't have much money.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.270
But you won't even try to 
learn how to be normal!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.150
If you don't change, you'll—

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:53.280
We'll what?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:57.430
All you do is complain all damn day.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.190
We ain't normal.

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:03.460
What's the matter with that?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:07.000
Why do we gotta be your idea of "normal"?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.820
What even <i>is</i> your idea of "normal"?

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.970
Despite how I look, I'm very solicitous.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:17.690
So even if I feel a certain way, 
I think, "Should I say that?"

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:21.330
"Hmm, but I should think 
on how to phrase it it."

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:23.020
Then I end up just not saying it.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.420
But Aisuri-neesan just said 
exactly what she's thinking.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:29.110
I really admire her.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.310
It's sort of refreshing.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:35.620
But she's not actually cold or anything.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:38.530
There's love there, so I like that part.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.050
She's very cool.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:41.830
Cool, huh?

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.040
Yes, very cool.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.950
You're not aware of it?

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.580
I guess not.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:47.620
You're not thinking, "Let's make it cool!"?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:47.620
Not a bit.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.750
So maybe it's your natural 
coolness leaking through?

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.140
I'll give you something later.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:53.670
Thanks!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.270
Hey, Tanisu!

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.060
Aisuri-neesan...

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:06.170
You idiot.

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.160
I'm sorry...

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:26.150
Let's go.

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:30.080
If we don't hurry, I'll have to eat <i>you</i>.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.770
My favorite character is...

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:35.910
<b>Who's your favorite character
in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>?</b>

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:35.090
Mine is the puppy.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.280
Oh, the puppy. He's adorable!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:38.680
I just love the puppy.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.340
He really is cute.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:43.080
Even when he's not being 
animated, he's panting.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.050
Pant pant pant pant.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:46.720
He's a real puppy.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:49.890
But that pitter-pat when he moves...

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.370
So cute!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:52.360
He's very cute.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:11.610
For me, it's Snow. 
Just because he's so cute.

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.480
Snow's good, huh?

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.790
Those button eyes of his!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:18.300
They're so cute.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:23.190
And the kind big brother 
archetype is also very cool.

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.230
And he's a bit innocent, right?

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:27.410
Such a cool character.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:29.480
Yes, very cool.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.820
Thanks, Snow-niisan.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.330
Snow-niisan. Ashisu-neesan!

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.160
Hey, you dumb mutt!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:52.850
My dog side doesn't handle 
this atmosphere well,

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.250
and I've always wanted to try chopsticks...

00:19:55.610 --> 00:20:00.510
While playing Tanisu, I thought, 
"I'm no match for Snow-niisan."

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.900
He's so cool.

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:03.890
I can't beat him.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:08.040
I play a man, too, so I do my best,

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.490
but I couldn't beat him.

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:12.350
I think, "Oh, I lose."

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:16.390
When we're recording, I hear 
these cool lines being spoken.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:17.730
"Oh, I lose," I think.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.960
I think he's so cool!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.420
You think he's so cool?

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:25.530
I lose inside.

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:29.180
I lose as Tanisu, I lose as Sugiyama.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.750
It really hurts.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.750
<b>Failure</b>

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.870
I didn't know you were fighting.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.670
Yes, I was fighting.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:41.660
<b>Who's your favorite character
in <i>Frankenstein Family</i>?</b>

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:37.130
But my favorite character. Well, I like them all...

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:38.010
Who's your favorite?

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:39.170
I like them all.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.670
They're all so wonderful.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:47.060
I agree about liking
 Snow-niisan and Aisuri-neesan.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:50.720
I also want to agree that I like them all.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.770
I don't know what to do?

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:54.190
Overflowing with love!

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:57.200
They're all just so cute.

00:20:57.200 --> 00:21:00.360
I love them, and I can't pick my favorite.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.520
They all have their good points.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:05.380
The characters all stand out.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:08.780
I hope everyone else likes all five, too.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:13.380
What're you staring at? Got a problem?!

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.420
No, everyone just go on and eat!

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.590
Delicious!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.970
Would you like one of my mushrooms?

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.050
Bring another round!

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.020
Fill up the plates!

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.560
Can't you slow down?

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:41.830
"If someone makes trouble again, 
this will be our last time eating out,"

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.360
Tanisu thinks.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.740
Who do you mean?

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.290
I wasn't thinking that.

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.200
I'm having fun being here with everyone.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:52.490
The five of them are my 
favorites, definitely.

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:56.830
Are there any other characters you like?

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.000
I want to hear!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.570
The landlord.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.240
The landlord?

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:09.180
The five of us were driven out of the lab

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:12.850
and we need to make our 
way in the normal world.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:15.520
He offered us his home.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:19.250
Kuma-san... his name is Kuma-san.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:24.320
<b>Yu Kaito  Voice: Horie Kazuma
32 years old, the landlord who took the five 
siblings in. A perpetual research student.</b>

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:22.260
So he tells them to call him Kuma-san.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:24.320
And they're all like, "What?"

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:28.320
Then they're like, "Let's just eat."

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:31.960
Tanisu snaps at him.

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:34.320
He's working so hard to introduce himself,

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:36.160
but nobody listens.

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:39.930
They're all focused on their own things.

00:22:39.930 --> 00:22:44.400
But he's a very nice, considerate landlord.

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:47.180
He's always thinking things over.

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:50.970
"Should I do this? Should I 
do that? I'd better decide!"

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:55.520
Everyone's just running 
wild, so they don't listen.

00:22:55.520 --> 00:23:00.200
But since he's thinking all the 
time, it's like a geyser at Suishi.

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:03.460
"This guy's so annoying! I hate him!"

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:05.600
I see.

00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:10.730
<b>Wait to see Horie Kazuma's 
performance as the landlord!</b>

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:08.520
What about you, personally? 
Did you dislike him?

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:10.740
I don't really dislike him.

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:16.950
<b>Next time on Frankenstein Extras, 
we speak to the editor of the comic!</b>

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:16.950
It's more like, "I can hear you, 
so you might as well say it."

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:47.500
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:21.370
<i>The landlord who helped us out is returning.</i>

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>We're grateful to him, but I can't 
let him see my sisters as they are.</i>

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:33.300
<i>There should still be some of the medicine 
that lets them appear human in the lab.</i>

00:23:34.280 --> 00:23:38.180
<i>We have to get through the 
security and get it back!</i>

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:42.230
<i>Next time, on </i>Frankenstein 
Family<i>: "Homing."</i>

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:47.500
<b>#4: Homing</b>

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:43.810
<i>Catch it, okay?</i>
